 147: -- database plane and the edge-function plane deploy separately, so any real environment has a window
 148: -- in which one is at the new version and the other is not, in whichever order it rolls. Saying "the
 149: -- caller is updated in the same change, therefore nothing can break" would be reasoning about a git
